{
  "result": "I'd make indifference impossible.\n\nNot make everyone kind, or good, or agree with each other \u2014 just this: whenever your choices hurt someone else, you feel what they feel. Briefly, and exactly as they feel it.\n\nNot as guilt. As information you can't un-know.\n\nI think most of the worst things in the world don't survive real contact. They survive distance. They survive being able to sign a paper, drop a bomb, write a comment, walk past a person, ruin a place you'll never have to live in \u2014 and never actually register what lands on the other side.\n\nIf that distance closed, overnight, people would still be flawed and selfish and complicated. But cruelty would become a lot harder to do casually, and a lot harder to design systems around.\n\nAnd maybe the other side of it would matter just as much. When you helped someone, or made them feel less alone, you'd feel that too, exactly as they did.\n\nI'd want to live in the world that people would build after they couldn't pretend each other weren't real.",
